:false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":true,"price":null},{"id":58489,"botanicalName":"<em>Pyrus</em> <em>communis</em> 'Beurré Alexandre Lucas' (D)","entityDescription":"A deciduous tree reaching 8m. It has glossy green leaves which become yellow in autumn. White blossom in spring develops into early-season pears with a conical shape. The ripe colour is golden green with a slight rosy blush and distinct russet lenticels (markings which are raised pores on the trunk). In storage, they have a tendency to decay in the core whilst looking perfect on the outside","image":"vima04487.jpg","commonName":"pear 'Beurré Alexandre Lucas'","nurseriesCount":2,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":true,"price":null},{"id":84654,"botanicalName":"<em>Pyrus</em> <em>communis</em> 'Beurré Clairgeau' (C)","entityDescription":"A compact, upright tree with shiny, rounded leaves and white blossom in spring. The medium-to-large, conical, cooking pears have rough, russetted, golden-brown to yellow skin with an orange-red blush, and firm, gritty, white, rather dry flesh with a musky flavour. Pick in mid-autumn and use to late autumn; crops well, but fruit often poor quality in UK conditions. Not self-fertile, in pollination group 2","image":"","commonName":"pear 'Beurré Clairgeau'","nurseriesCount":1,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":true,"price":null},{"id":75640,"botanicalName":"<em>Pyrus</em> <em>communis</em> 'Beurré Superfin' (D)","entityDescription":"A cultivar with a fine, melting, scented flesh with slightly rough, russetted, pale green and yellow skin. A high quality pear that needs a warm, sheltered site. Pollination group 3. Season of use late September and October","image":"RHS_RHS-0008581_9580.JPG","commonName":"pear 'Beurré Superfin'","nurseriesCount":4,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":true,"price":null},{"id":44925,"botanicalName":"<em>Pyrus</em> <em>communis</em> 'Beurré d'Amanlis' (D)","entityDescription":"A medium-sized, upright tree with shiny, oval leaves and white blossom in spring. The medium-sized, pear-shaped fruit have rough, dull green skin with variable russetting and slightly gritty, fairly juicy, pale yellow flesh with a pleasant, mild flavour. Pick and use in early autumn; reliable and hardy, but there are many better dessert pears. Not self-fertile, triploid, in pollination group 2","image":"","commonName":"pear 'Beurré d'Amanlis'","nurseriesCount":1,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":true,"price":null},{"id":64799,"botanicalName":"<em>Pyrus</em> <em>communis</em> 'Clapp's Favourite' (D)","entityDescription":"A medium-sized tree with rather drooping branches, long, oval, shiny leaves and white blossom in spring. Smooth-skinned fruit are pale green to pale yellow with bright red flushing, and pale yellow, juicy flesh with a mild, pleasant flavour. Pick and use in late summer. Not self-fertile, in pollination group 4","image":"","commonName":"pear 'Clapp's Favourite'","nurseriesCount":8,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":true,"price":null},{"id":229846,"botanicalName":"<em>Pyrus</em> <em>communis</em> 'Delwinor'","entityDescription":"A medium-sized, very hardy tree which can flower twice in spring so will normally crop well even if frost damages early blossom. Fruit are broadly conical, with russet skin, and sweet, soft, juicy flesh. Pick from early autumn and store to late winter, using early fruit for cooking, later ones for desert. Partially self-fertile, pollination group 2","image":"","commonName":"pear [Invincible]","nurseriesCount":11,"synonymParentPlantId":226319,"synonymParentPlantName":"<em>Pyrus</em> <em>communis</em> <span s